0pt;font-weight:700;line-height:112%"&gt;10&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;&#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style="padding:2px 1pt 2px 0;text-align:right;vertical-align:top"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:112%"&gt;%&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:0 1pt"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="2" style="padding:2px 0 2px 1pt;text-align:right;vertical-align:top"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;110.8&#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style="padding:2px 1pt 2px 0;text-align:right;vertical-align:top"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:0 1pt"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="2" style="padding:2px 0 2px 1pt;text-align:right;vertical-align:top"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;12&#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style="padding:2px 1pt 2px 0;text-align:right;vertical-align:top"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;%&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%"&gt;Gas Loaned to Customers&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify;text-indent:36pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;Natural gas price volatility can cause changes in credit risk related to gas loaned to customers, including affiliated customers. As of December 31, 2025, the amount of gas owed to Gulf South due to gas imbalances and gas loaned under PAL and certain firm service agreements was approximately 4.94 trillion British thermal units (TBtu). Assuming an average market price during December 2025 of $3.90 per million British thermal unit (MMBtu), the market value of that gas was approximately $19.3 million. As of December 31, 2024, the amount of gas owed to Gulf South due to gas imbalances and gas loaned under PAL and certain firm service agreements was approximately 1.5 TBtu. Assuming an average market price during December 2024 of $2.98 per MMBtu, the market value of that gas was approximately $4.5 million. If any significant customer should have credit or financial problems resulting in a delay or failure to pay for services provided or repay the gas owed to Gulf South, it could have a material adverse effect on Gulf South&#8217;s financial condition, results of operations and cash flows.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%"&gt;Note 8: Related Party Transactions &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify;text-indent:36pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;Gulf South makes advances to or receives advances from Boardwalk Pipelines under the cash management program described in Note 2. As of December 31, 2025 and 2024, there were no advances due to or from Boardwalk Pipelines as the amounts were settled.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify;text-indent:36pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;Texas Gas, a wholly owned operating subsidiary of Boardwalk Pipelines, provides services through the gas management system to support the commercial operations of Gulf South. Texas Gas charges Gulf South licensing fees under a software license agreement, which has a term of one year and is automatically renewed annually unless the agreement is terminated by Gulf South with a 30-day advance notice or by Texas Gas at any time. Gulf South incurred fixed and variable charges related to these services of $17.1 million and $18.3 million for the years ended December 31, 2025 and 2024. The fixed charges were derived from a cost of service model, including a rate of return, and the variable charges were based on maintenance costs incurred. These charges were allocated amongst the users of the gas management system based on an allocation methodology developed from certain commercial criteria. Management believes the assumptions used and allocations made were on a reasonable basis.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify;text-indent:36pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;Boardwalk Pipelines provides certain management and other services to Gulf South, including corporate services from Loews. Gulf South incurred charges related to these services of $10.5 million and $9.9 million for the years ended December 31, 2025 and 2024.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify;text-indent:36pt"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify;text-indent:36pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;For the year ended December 31, 2025, an associated company transferred land with a carrying amount of $0.5 million to Gulf South. The transfer was accounted for as a non-cash contribution from Boardwalk Pipelines. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify;text-indent:36pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;Excluding the asset transfer above, Gulf South made non-cash distributions to Boardwalk Pipelines of $508.4 million and $401.9 million for the years ended December 31, 2025 and 2024, and Boardwalk Pipelines made non-cash contributions to Gulf South of $5.6 million for the year ended December 31, 2025. For the year ended December 31, 2024, Boardwalk Pipelines made no non-cash contributions to Gulf South.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify;text-indent:36pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;Amounts applicable to PAL services provided to an associated company or transportation services received from an associated company recorded on Gulf South's Statements of Income were as follows (in millions):&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:center"&gt;&lt;table style="border-collapse:collapse;display:inline-table;margin-bottom:5pt;vertical-align:text-bottom;width:64.732%"&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="width:1.0%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:68.095%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.1%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.1%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:1.639%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.1%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:1.0%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:12.463%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.1%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.1%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:1.639%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.1%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:1.0%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:12.464%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.1%"/&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="p